From abe1af69abde60ad915a3393e4db523aeee7ae2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:32:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 268/270] hdmi.media_addon: the HDMI port as a video output
 node

The node shows in the video outputs of the Media preferences and in
Cortex. What is sent to it fills the whole HDMI screen while the
panel keeps the desktop: frames are copied into two overlay buffers
of the display driver in turn. Its parameters turn the HDMI output on
and off and set the resolution choice, plain DVI and a stronger
signal, in the tegra_dc driver settings; the status line shows the
screen and its mode.

It replaces the separate HDMI preferences application, which goes.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
